# ORCLOOZE: the shark that only swims, and the slime that only spreads (M16.5).
#
# These two creatures are opposites in what makes them comparable. A shark seeks
# exactly like a lion (P1 9 forces the seek half of `P1 < Random(10)`), so it is
# only draw-free while it shares the player's row or column — the beast.scn rule.
# A slime draws nothing at all: ElementSlimeTick counts P1 up to P2 and then
# walks the four NeighborDelta directions in a fixed order, so it is comparable
# wherever the player stands.
#
# Ooze Bay, row 13 — the shark channel. ElementSharkTick moves onto E_WATER and
# nothing else, and attacks only E_PLAYER, so the same seek that carries it down
# the channel stops dead at the shoreline:
#   20,13  a shark in fifteen squares of water, seeking west along the player's
#          own row. It swims to 6,13, the last wet square, and then attacks the
#          player standing dry at 5,13 — 100 health -> 90, and the attack kills
#          it (DamageStat on the attacker).
#   30,13  a second shark in its own pool, with dry land at 29,13 between it and
#          everything else. Its seek points west at that land every tick and it
#          never moves; once the player leaves row 13 both of the directions
#          CalcDirectionSeek can return are dry, so it stays put whatever the
#          draw says. That is the refusal, and it is what makes the rest of the
#          scenario safe to walk around in.
#
# Ooze Bay, row 8 — the slime tunnel, one square wide between two walls. The
# width is the point: NeighborDeltaX/Y is (north, south, west, east), so in a
# horizontal tunnel the first two directions are walls, the third MOVES the
# slime west and leaves a breakable in its own colour behind it, and the fourth
# ADDS a second slime to the east carrying the same P2. From then on each front
# has one walkable neighbour and simply advances, so the tunnel becomes a wall
# of breakables growing from the middle outward at one square per two slime
# ticks (P1 counts to P2 = 1 before every spread).
#
# Both of the ways a slime can end are here, and they need two different slimes
# because a spreading one cannot be caught by hand:
#   6,11   a DORMANT slime (P2 250, so P1 never counts far enough to spread)
#          sitting where the player walks past it. ElementSlimeTouch damages the
#          SLIME, not the player — the slime's stat is removed and its square
#          becomes a breakable in its own colour, at no health cost. It is the
#          one creature in ZZT whose touch is free, and the player is left
#          standing in front of a breakable instead of walking through.
#   the tunnel fronts die the other way ElementSlimeTick can end: no walkable
#          neighbour at all, so the slime turns into a breakable where it
#          stands. The east front runs out of tunnel at 41,8; the west front is
#          cornered by the player standing in its path, which is exactly why the
#          touch station cannot be done with a moving slime — the moment the
#          player is adjacent, the slime has nowhere left to go and dies on its
#          own before a walk-in can land.
world ORCLOOZE
seed 0
phase
boot 240
capture title
play
# Ooze Hub: unpause and cross the east border opening at 60,13.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture arrive
# Walk to the shoreline at 5,13 and wait for the shark to come to us.
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture shoreline
settle 30
capture shark-closing
settle 30
capture shark-hit
# Up the dry western edge, walking into the dormant slime on the way.
move up
move up
move right
capture slime-touched
move up
move up
move up
capture tunnel-mouth
# East into the tunnel, in front of the advancing west front.
move right
move right
move right
capture slime-met
settle 20
capture slime-cornered
settle 60
capture slime-spent
